# Node / frontend (for the future frontend/ workspace)
#
# The Python-convention `lib/` rule above matches a *directory* at any depth, so
# it swallows first-party source: frontend/src/lib/, the tests tree that mirrors
# it, and the gate's own ci/lib/. A new file under any of them is silently
# untracked — never committed, never run, with nothing on screen to say so.
#
# Each negation re-includes the directory and nothing more. That is deliberate:
# `lib/` excluded the directory, and git will not evaluate rules for files under
# an excluded directory, so un-excluding it is enough to make its contents
# visible again — and they are then matched against every other rule as usual.
# A `!<dir>/**` companion would instead re-include every descendant outright and
# override the artifact and secret rules above it, which is how
# ci/lib/__pycache__/x.pyc, ci/lib/x.pyc and ci/lib/.env became trackable.
!frontend/src/lib/
!frontend/tests/lib/
# The trees mirror each other, so a lib/ segment can appear at any depth —
# frontend/tests/features/lib/widget.test.ts is missed by the root-level
# negations alone.
!frontend/tests/**/lib/
!frontend/src/**/lib/
!ci/lib/
node_modules/
# Generated dependency-cache fingerprints written by ci/checks/node.sh
# and ci/checks/python.sh.
.ci-gate/
.next/
out/
build/
.turbo/
